> > feature.
> > I would strongly recommend you use the inlabru package interface instead of
> > plain INLA for this, as inlabru removes the need for direct inla.stack()
> > calls, and nlabru handles the inla.surv response objects automatically
> > (precisely using the 'responses# argument to inla.stack() internally).
> >
> > Manual use of inla.stack() should be considered a legacy feature that's still
> > visible only to support old existing code. New code that would have needed it
> > in the past (before inlabru 2.11.1 from 2024-07-01) is much better off using
> > inlabru instead, as that's what it's for (it's one of the several reasons
> > inlabru exists).
> >
> > Finn
