Message-ID: <8Hp7_lDVaWU.dN-KdOl_BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <8Hp7_lDVaWU.prtGGo9_BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <8Hp7_lDVaWU.prtGGo9_BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/8Hp7_lDVaWU/m/dN-KdOl_BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The glibc issue is fixed by installing the ubuntu2204 build,

inla.binary.install()

and chose ubuntu-22.04

please use the recent testing-version of INLA and R-4.6.

the 'stiles' issue is due to different version of the R-INLA and the binary that
it runs, syncronizing these will fix the issue.

let me know if this does not work

best
H

