And it also occurs if I import HTC-run INLA outputs to my local PC and try running `inla.group.cv <http://inla.group.cv>()` from there.
May I please ask if there is anything I can do in the script to make `inla.group.cv <http://inla.group.cv>()` work in my environment?

I attach the reproducible R script, the .err and the .out files, but I can provide more objects if needed (e.g. the INLA output).

Thank you in advance,
Best
LC

